From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.speech: SpeechRecognizer hears speech through the system's engine.

RecognizeAsync gave an empty TimeoutExceeded result: there was no recognition engine. Stained Glass OS has
one, its voice typing (sg-dictate: Parakeet on the CPU, the model installed with the system); a unixlib
runs it as the program's own user ("sg-dictate --listen --once", at most ten seconds, the recognizer's
language when it is one the engine knows) and reads what was said. Dictation gives the words with High
confidence; with list constraints, what was said must be one of their phrases (letter case, spaces and
end punctuation aside): the phrase as written and its constraint, otherwise Rejected with no text. With no
engine, no model or nothing heard, the result stays TimeoutExceeded.
---
